  },
  "1046355": {
    "ENU": "Large ore:"
  },
  "1046356": {
    "ENU": "If you are leaving the mansion, you should learn about the Radar Map."
  },
  "1046357": {
    "ENU": "The Radar Map (or Overhead View) can be opened by pressing 'ALT-R' on your keyboard. It shows your immediate surroundings from a bird's eye view."
  },
  "1046358": {
    "ENU": "Pressing ALT-R twice, will enlarge the Radar Map a little.  The map shows you your immediate surroundings from a bird's eye view."
  },
  "1046359": {
    "ENU": "You can close the map by right clicking on it.  Use the Radar Map often as you travel throughout the world to familiarize yourself with your surroundings."
  },
  "1046360": {
    "ENU": "Why are you giving me this?  You need to make pickaxes!"
  },
  "1046361": {
    "ENU": "You have not made two pickaxes.  Come back and show me your work when you have both completed."
  },
  "1046362": {
    "ENU": "Yes"
  },
  "1046363": {
    "ENU": "No"
  },
  "1046364": {
    "ENU": "Remember that context menus can be called up by single left clicking something (or shift-left click if you have changed the option)."
  },
  "1046365": {
    "ENU": "After you have indicated to the vendor that you wish to purchase something, you will be shown a list of the goods they have to offer."
  },
  "1046366": {
    "ENU": "Speaking of context menus, you can bring up the status of your quest by bringing up your avatar's own context menu (single left, or shift-left click yourself)."
  },
  "1046367": {
    "ENU": "Choose the 'Quest Log' option, and any information pertinent to your current quest status will be shown to you."
  },
  "1046368": {
    "ENU": "To help you find the location of the treasure, you should become familiar with the Radar Map."
  },
  "1046369": {
    "ENU": "The teleporter to the caves is against the north wall of this room."
  },
  "1046370": {
    "ENU": "May good luck and fortune guide your way."
  },
  "1046371": {
    "ENU": "Once you emerge from the Moongate, the city will be roughly to the north.  It should not be difficult to find.  Find Aegis and speak with him once you are in the city.."
  },
  "1046372": {
    "ENU": "Actually, before you can spend this money, you will have to take the check to a bank and cash it."
  },
  "1046373": {
    "ENU": "NPC shop keepers do not accept checks as payment.  Checks are a handy way to transport large sums of money without having to lug all that gold around."
  },
  "1046374": {
    "ENU": "Cashing a check is very easy.  All you have to do is locate a NPC Banker or Minter, walk near them and say the word 'Bank'."
  },
  "1046375": {
    "ENU": "Place the check into your bank box and double click it to cash it.  Bankers and Minters can be found inside of banks across the world."
  },
  "1046376": {
    "ENU": "There is a bank not too far from here, Southeast of this shop, actually.  Banks are often crowded with people conducting business."
  },
  "1046377": {
    "ENU": "Go now to cash your check.  The person cashing your check will explain the details of Britannia's banking system to you."
  },
  "1046378": {
    "ENU": "Ah! Thank you noble adventurer!  I have accepted your check and cashed it for you.  The cash can be found in your bank box."
  },
  "1046379": {
    "ENU": "To open your bank box, you must be near a Banker or Minter and say the word 'Bank'."
  },
  "1046380": {
    "ENU": "Of course you can also open your bank box by using a Minter's or Banker's context menu."
  },
  "1046381": {
    "ENU": "Bank boxes in Britannia are special in that the goods you place in to a bank box anywhere, can be accessed from your bank box anywhere else in the land."
  },
  "1046382": {
    "ENU": "That is to say, your bank box, along with any goods you placed into it,  is accessible from any bank in the land."
  },
  "1046383": {
    "ENU": "The safest place for any of your goods, is your bank box.  No one can access it except for you."
  },
  "1046384": {
    "ENU": "That's pretty much all there is to banking.  I bet you are eager to explore the world, so I won't hold you up any longer."
  },
  "1046385": {
    "ENU": "I've no tasks for you to complete, and you are free to adventure in the world on your own."
  },
  "1046386": {
    "ENU": "May your bank box overflow with the spoils of your adventures.  We shall no doubt see each other again."
  },
  "1046387": {
    "ENU": "Farewell."
  },
  "1046388": {
    "ENU": "Locate the bank and find the NPC Banker (or Minter) inside.  Then, say the word 'Bank' and place your check into your bank box and double click it."
  },
  "1046389": {
    "ENU": "To make it easier to find the Treasure, be sure to use your radar map."
  },
  "1046390": {
    "ENU": "To make your attack, you will most likely wish to use your magical powers, so allow me to give you a brief explanation of magic."
  },
  "1046391": {
    "ENU": "Most often, spells start out as scrolls written by either NPC or Player scribes.  Once a spell has been successfully scribed, you have two choices:"
  },
  "1046392": {
    "ENU": "One: You can cast the spell by using (double click) the scroll.  No spell reagents (ingredients) are required to cast spells from scrolls. Casting from a scroll consumes the scroll."
  },
  "1046393": {
    "ENU": "Two: You can drop the scroll on to your spellbook where it will be permanently written.  You can then cast the spell from your spellbook any time you wish."
  },
  "1046394": {
    "ENU": "To cast a spell from a spellbook, the necessary reagents are required (listed with the spell in your spellbook). "
  },
  "1046395": {
    "ENU": "Casting spells from a spellbook AND casting spells from scrolls requires a certain amount of mana. The actual amount of mana required differs from circle to circle."
  },
  "1046396": {
    "ENU": "The 1st circle of spells is the easiest of spells to cast (and also has the least mana requirement) whilst 8th circle spells are difficult even for a Grandmaster Mage."
  },
  "1046397": {
    "ENU": "To actually cast a spell from your spellbook, you must first open your spellbook (double click).  This opens the book to the 1st & 2nd circle spells."
  },
  "1046398": {
    "ENU": "You can turn pages by single clicking the corner in the top right hand side of the spellbook, or you can single click on the circled numbers on the bottom to jump to specific circle."
  },
  "1046399": {
    "ENU": "You can double click any of the spell names to make an attempt at casting that spell.  To see a spell's reagent requirements, single click on the spell name."
  },
  "1046400": {
    "ENU": "Single clicking on a spell name will give you all the details of the spell.  You can see the aforementioned reagent requirements as well as the spell's icon."
  },
  "1046401": {
    "ENU": "Another way of casting a spell is to click on that spell's spell icon.  You can drag any spell's icon off of the book and place it anywhere in the game window."
  },
  "1046402": {
    "ENU": "Once a spell icon is in the game window, it will stay there even if you close the spellbook.  This is an easy way to set up many spells for quick casting."
  },
  "1046403": {
    "ENU": "Before going into battle, you should always check your reagent supply and make sure you have your spell icons set up."
  },
  "1046404": {
    "ENU": "You now have enough Mandrake in your pack to complete your task for Uzeraan.  Find Uzeraan and give him 75 mandrake roots by dragging them onto him."
  },
  "1046405": {
    "ENU": "You have enough Mandrake in your pack to complete your task for Uzeraan.  Find Uzeraan and give him 75 mandrake roots by dragging them onto him."
  },
  "1046406": {
    "ENU": "I have drawn you a picture of what the Reagent Shop sign looks like (left).   Remember that you can also look at (single click) shop signs to read them."
  },
  "1046407": {
    "ENU": "Marking runes is easy.  I'll give you a quick explanation of how it works, then I would advise that you mark a rune somewhere around my mansion so you can return quickly."
  },
  "1046408": {
    "ENU": "To mark a rune, you must stand in the place where you wish to appear when casting the 'Recall' or 'Gate' spell."
  },
  "1046409": {
    "ENU": "Then you cast the mark spell (either from a scroll or your spellbook, as I have explained earlier).  Once the spell is cast you will get a targeting cursor."
  },
  "1046410": {
    "ENU": "Target the rune you wish to mark and single click it.  If your spell is successful, the rune will sparkle and will from then on be 'marked'."
  },
  "1046411": {
    "ENU": "Looking at the rune (single click) will give you the description of the rune.  If you wish to change the default description, simply double click the rune."
  },
  "1046412": {
    "ENU": "Once you have double clicked the rune, you will get a text prompt.  Enter the new description and press the [enter] key on your keyboard."
  },
  "1046413": {
    "ENU": "By naming all of your runes to something that is meaningful to you, you can keep your rune library organized and easy to use."
  },
  "1046414": {
    "ENU": "the remains of ~1_NAME~"
  },
  "1046415": {
    "ENU": "~1_bulkname~ / ~2_amountreq~ ~3_intamount~ / ~4_excep~ / ~5_ingottype~ / ~6_itemname~"
  },
  "1046416": {
    "ENU": "During combat it is important to keep an eye on your hit points.  Should they ever drop below 0, you will die."
  },
  "1046417": {
    "ENU": "To bring up your status bar, single click yourself and drag away from your avatar.  Double click the status bar to see details."
  },
  "1046418": {
    "ENU": "If your health drops too low, you should heal yourself with bandages or healing potions.  Heal yourself often, and you should have no trouble surviving."
  },
  "1046419": {
    "ENU": "One more thing before you depart for battle:"
  },
  "1046420": {
    "ENU": "You have found a Moongate.  Remember to choose 'Moonglow' as your destination when you step into the gate."
  },
  "1046421": {
    "ENU": "Moonglow is where Aegis is waiting for you in his shop."
  },
  "1046422": {
    "ENU": "Congratulations! You've completed all of your quests!"
  },
  "1046423": {
    "ENU": "I can open a Moongate for you from here to an area close to the Moongate that can take you to the city of Moonglow."
  },
  "1046424": {
    "ENU": "I only have runes marked for near the Moongate, but the sextant will help you find the rest of the way."
  },
  "1046425": {
    "ENU": "Aegis' Shop"
  },
  "1046426": {
    "ENU": "I have drawn you a picture to the left of what the sign on Aegis' Shop looks like. It should help you find it a little easier."
  },
  "1046427": {
    "ENU": "You do not have enough reagents to safely go on.  You should acquire at least 35 of each reagent."
  },
  "1046428": {
    "ENU": "There are 8 types of reagent: Mandrake, Nightshade, Black Pearl, Sulfurous Ash, Spider's Silk, Garlic, Ginseng and Bloodmoss."
  },
  "1046429": {
    "ENU": "The caves tend to be dark, so be sure to cast the 'Night Sight' spell on yourself if you have trouble seeing."
  },
