  },
  "1073300": {
    "ENU": "Library Friends - Quotes from the pen of Sherry the Mouse"
  },
  "1073301": {
    "ENU": "Oft have I wished that stranger would return."
  },
  "1073302": {
    "ENU": "A shard of a universe is a powerful thing."
  },
  "1073303": {
    "ENU": "Aid the nobility that resideth in human heart."
  },
  "1073304": {
    "ENU": "Yet sometimes one must sacrifice a pawn to save a king."
  },
  "1073305": {
    "ENU": "Even pawns have lives and loves at home, my lord."
  },
  "1073306": {
    "ENU": "But I am but a mouse, and none hear me."
  },
  "1073307": {
    "ENU": "We must bring the shards into harmony, so that they resonate in such a manner that matches the original universe."
  },
  "1073308": {
    "ENU": "Suddenly the shutters blew open, and Lord British fell to the ground, one hand shileding his eyes."
  },
  "1073309": {
    "ENU": "I witnessed them all from my tiny mousehole."
  },
  "1073310": {
    "ENU": "Library Friends - Quotes from the pen of Wyrd Beastmaster"
  },
  "1073311": {
    "ENU": "I have not much to tell about dragons."
  },
  "1073312": {
    "ENU": "The fireball was massive enough to light a city I should surmise."
  },
  "1073313": {
    "ENU": "The sole time I approached one with an eye towards taming it, my initial attempts at calming it met with failure."
  },
  "1073314": {
    "ENU": "...the dragon suddenly whirled as if in a panic, ran a short distance, took off into the air, then transformed into a whirlwind. "
  },
  "1073315": {
    "ENU": "I never did discover the exact cause of this strange behavior except to assume that it was not typical for this reptilian species."
  },
  "1073316": {
    "ENU": "Hence my basic advice to those who seek to tame a dragon-be sure that thou hast mastered the twin skills of taming animals, and running away very fast."
  },
  "1073317": {
    "ENU": "Library Friends - Quotes from the pen of Mercenary Justin"
  },
  "1073318": {
    "ENU": "Be wary of a brazier that giveth warning when approached: thou canst use it to summon deadly creatures."
  },
  "1073319": {
    "ENU": "Deceit was once a temple to forgotten powers of old."
  },
  "1073320": {
    "ENU": "Do not investigate the iron maidens too closely, for they make suck you within them!"
  },
  "1073321": {
    "ENU": "There is one place where a deadly trap can only be disarmed by making use of a statue that cleverly conceals a lever."
  },
  "1073322": {
    "ENU": "Oft one encounters the deadly exploding toadstool; the ones in Deceit are deadlier than most, as they explode continually."
  },
  "1073323": {
    "ENU": "Likewise, the very pools of water and slime on the floor may poisen thee."
  },
  "1073324": {
    "ENU": "The dungeon is mystically linked by crystal balls placed in different locations."
  },
  "1073325": {
    "ENU": "Deceit was once a temple to forgotten powers of old."
  },
  "1073326": {
    "ENU": "Wisps are the most intelligent of the nonhuman races inhabiting Britannia."
  },
  "1073327": {
    "ENU": "Library Friends - Quotes from the pen of Heigel of Moonglow"
  },
  "1073328": {
    "ENU": "The wispish language seems to only contain one vowel, the letter Y."
  },
  "1073329": {
    "ENU": "The average word in wispish seems to consist of three phonemes and three glottal stops, plus possibly a pitch shift."
  },
  "1073330": {
    "ENU": "Wisps do make use of what sounds to us like pitch and emphasis shifts similar to exclamations and questions."
  },
  "1073331": {
    "ENU": "Some have speculated that what we are analyzing is in fact nothing more than the very air crackling near the wisp's glow, and not language, but this is of course unlikely."
  },
  "1073332": {
    "ENU": "Her name was Leyla, she said, and her hair was braided wild with creepers and thorns."
  },
  "1073333": {
    "ENU": "Her provenance, she told me over nights illuminated by campfires, was once the city of Trinsic."
  },
  "1073334": {
    "ENU": "Oft have I wondered of the boy named Japheth, and whether he remembers a girl who lived in sandstone walls."
  },
  "1073335": {
    "ENU": "'Twas a fearful run, and I came to the road to Yew with welts and scratches run rampant crost my skin, but I did not see her again."
  },
  "1073336": {
    "ENU": "He had sandy hair like thee, and I dreamt as a child of holding his hand and sharing flavored ice. His name was Japheth."
  },
  "1073337": {
    "ENU": "...her smile seemed full of teeth sharper than a human ought to have, for the tale of orcish raising had struck fear into the marrow of my bones."
  },
  "1073338": {
    "ENU": "Library Friends - Quotes from the pen of Horace, Trader"
  },
