  "1114495": {
    "ENU": "<DIV ALIGN=CENTER>RENOWN</DIV><P>Renown amongst your warrior peers is gained on the field of battle. You will gain recognition for harming foes, healing compatriots, sneaking amongst your enemies, rooting out spies and concealed traps, and for fighting for control of sigils.</P><P>Additionally, you gain more recognition for fighting in larger battles and for fighting against larger enemy forces.</P><P>The system displays numerical ratings showing how you perform compared to the average for all current Faction members. Your rating descriptions depend on your ratings but are capped by your average activity level.</P><P>Ranks are awarded by renown but are capped by activity level; if you do not fight in battles you will eventually be known as a Deserter and will not receive any benefits from Faction membership.</P>"
  },
