  "1114791": {
    "ENU": " These are the basic elements to consider in assessing a weapon of which all warriors who regard themselves as more than mere mercenaries should be aware."
  },
  "1114792": {
    "ENU": " First and most obvious is the amount of damage that the weapon may do against unprotected flesh. While 'tis this which first attracts the attention of the novice, 'tis a deadly mistake to regard it as"
  },
  "1114793": {
    "ENU": "the sole value of a weapon. While it may prove devastating indeed as a means of causing damage, a weapon must also serve as stout shield when engaged in combat."
  },
  "1114794": {
    "ENU": " Hence the second issue to which to pay attention is the amount of protection that a weapon may offer. Pay close attention to the guard on it, if it be a blade, or the stoutness of its"
  },
  "1114795": {
    "ENU": "wood if it is a pole arm.<br><br> Oft related to this is the weight of a weapon, for a heavy weapon is more difficult to maneuver to block with, though it may do more"
  },
  "1114796": {
    "ENU": "damage to thy opponent.<br><br> If a weapon is too heavy for the wielder to move it freely, they should choose another and not attempt to prove their prowess by the size"
  },
  "1114797": {
    "ENU": "of their sword.<br><br> The reach of a weapon both increase its defensive ability, and renders it more useful in open spaces as it allows attack against the"
  },
  "1114798": {
    "ENU": "opponent without the need to close. But be aware of the limitations of thy weapon! For a weapon with great reach may be useless in close quarters, for lack of space to maneuver it. Should that"
  },
  "1114799": {
    "ENU": "dagger-wielding enemy close on thee and thy halberd, 'tis best to flee.<br><br> Lastly, a factor that must always be considered is the condition of the weapon. It might be a"
  },
  "1114800": {
    "ENU": "wondrous magical blade of surpassing sharpness and it may leap to block blows with a mind of its own. It also might be of such flimsy construction, or damaged to such an extent, that the first"
  },
  "1114801": {
    "ENU": "time it clangs against steel, 'twill shatter into useless shards.<br><br> Seek ye a good blacksmith should thy weapon become damaged, but be aware that their"
  },
  "1114802": {
    "ENU": "ministrations may simply make the matter worse.<br><br> While mages of some ability oft create magical weapons which enhance skill, are preternaturally sharp, or incinerate the"
  },
  "1114803": {
    "ENU": "enemy as they fall, to mind the greatest gift that they can grant a stout sword is to make it resistant to damage, for they own skill can make up the difference. Except for the fireball,"
  },
  "1114804": {
    "ENU": "but if the corpse is charred, then so will be the possessions, which maketh looting difficult!"
  },
  "1114805": {
    "ENU": " The dungeon known as Despise is in fact not a dungeon as such, but rather a large natural cave. Inhospitable and unfriendly to visitors, it is filled with damp spots where the deadly Exploding"
  },
  "1114806": {
    "ENU": "Red Spotted Toadstool grows in abundance.<br><br> According to the oldest of historical texts, in days gone by the cave was once the home of three separate tribes who"
  },
  "1114807": {
    "ENU": "had come to an accommodation with each other. Oddly enough, the three tribes were of dragons, lizard men, and rat men. While today few except extremists associated with Lord"
  },
  "1114808": {
    "ENU": "Blackthorn regard these latter two as being intelligent beings, apparently they have indeed fallen from a more evolved state over the years. "
  },
  "1114809": {
    "ENU": " 'Tis said that these three races did dwell in relative harmony within the vast cave, building when they required it, and trading amongst themselves if needed. "
  },
  "1114810": {
    "ENU": " But over time, something happened, and they were forced to withdraw from their society, until today thou mayst find individuals of each species within the dungeon, but never again as a civilization."
  },
  "1114811": {
    "ENU": " 'Tis also said that someday the three tribes may return to Despise, to once again inhabit it together.<br><br> Until then, nothing remains as token of this"
  },
  "1114812": {
    "ENU": "save an oddly intelligent skeleton, magically enchanted, that doth speak when questions are asked, and from whom I obtained these tales one day, when I was pursued by evil monsters and fled"
  },
  "1114813": {
    "ENU": "into his skeletal arms.<br><br> Fortunately, I escaped and lived to write it all down!"
  },
  "1114814": {
    "ENU": "You feel nether energy surge through you."
  },
  "1114815": {
    "ENU": "The chaotic nether bolt hits you particularly hard."
  },
  "1114816": {
    "ENU": "magic infused rubble"
  },
  "1114817": {
    "ENU": "The Slasher emits a powerful howl, shaking the very walls around you and suppressing your ability to move."
  },
  "1114818": {
    "ENU": "\"Sweet dreams\""
  },
  "1114819": {
    "ENU": "I will trade your non-stackable seeds or bag of seeds for stackable ones. BEWARE!!! If you cannot carry the bag, it will fall to the ground!"
  },
  "1114820": {
    "ENU": "Gargoyles have their own language, called Gargish. Gargoyles also have their own principles and Virtues."
  },
